2026-11-21T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2500) 'A face tracker that starts from speech and a headcam
 # uuid: 922504f0-5128-5fee-9baf-044b6fed425c
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-11-21T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2500) 'a face tracker for one wearer, from a headcam and speech to Unified Expressions.
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2500) 'the take format, the keypoint head, the face policy, and the Hailo front end.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2500) 'Can a muscle-driven policy track one person's face from a headcam and from speech, and also drive a persona that has no camera, with every model openly licensed and the face never stored?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2500) 'The pieces now exist in parts. A skin patch under small forces responds as a membrane should. A take file written by an Elixir DSL round-trips 200 random takes exactly, and OpenUSD 0.26.5 opens it. The headcam gives an upright 768 by 1024 frame. The Hailo-10H is rated 40 TOPS at INT4 and 20 at INT8. A keypoint head trained on synthetic renders scores 0.86 against a bar of 0.80 on held-out renders, in one run. No face muscle model or policy exists yet.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2500) 'Run the single build command in the take repository. It compiles, runs the tests, and has OpenUSD open a good take and refuse three broken ones.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2500) 'Measurements behind the face tracker plan
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2500) 'The goal is a VRCFT tracker for the operator's own face, headcam to Unified Expressions, by a MuscleMimic-style policy that also runs with any input masked (operator, 2026-11-21).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2500) '- English comes first, and the first slice is jaw and mouth from speech, driven by the TTS text and timing (operator, 2026-11-21).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2500) '- The operator's face is never stored or trained on. It is scored live in memory, and only numbers are written (operator, 2026-11-21).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2500) '- Stages exchange a take, one OpenUSD file. Take files are written in GDScript, C++ or an Elixir DSL, never Python (operator, 2026-11-21).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2500) '- Data and weights are Apache, MIT or CC0 (operator, 2026-11-22). Training data are renders and simulation.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2500) '- The policy is a guest ELF trained on the RTX 4090. Reflexive networks go to the Hailo-10H when they fit, at 4-bit or lower, and exactness does not block them (operator, 2026-11-21).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2500) '- RFD66606-2478 (ANNY-soma-x keypoints), whose keypoint head this one extends to the face.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2500) '- RFD66606-2327 (keypoints, supports and contacts), the generic keypoint vocabulary.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2500) '- RFD66606-2311 (serving Bonsai 2), the quantization route for the 2-bit goal.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2500) 'What was measured
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2500) 'Skin patch: a 9 by 9 grid, 5 millimetres apart (a little under a pencil's width) and 2 thick, border pinned, in MuJoCo 3.4.0 on CPU, stretch only. A free patch moved 6 to 23 millimetres, from about a pencil's width to a bit more than a penny's width. At 20 kilopascals an in-plane push of 2 millinewtons moved the centre 0.0756 millimetres (a tenth of a card's thickness), and 4 millinewtons moved it twice as far. Ten times stiffer gave ten times less. A normal push moved it 1.88 millimetres (a little more than a penny's thickness), and doubling the force gave 1.34 times that, near the 1.26 of a stretch-only membrane.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2500) 'Take format: 10 tests pass. 200 random takes, with quotes, newlines and non-Latin text, decode to exactly what was written, and a writer that rounds floats fails two tests. A second write never replaces a file. OpenUSD 0.26.5 in the usd guest opened the good take, read its layer data back, and refused a missing bracket, a half file and plain text.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2500) 'Hardware: the headcam opens only through the Media Foundation backend, upright, with the right eye closing on the image's left. Windows shows the Hailo-10H with firmware 5.5.0, and the compiler's TensorFlow and PyTorch both see the RTX 4090.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2500) 'Keypoint head: RF-DETR's keypoint preview, fine-tuned for 40 epochs on 120 synthetic head renders with 88 keypoints whose labels come from the mesh, seed 1, on the GPU only. A held-out test of 24 renders (1,992 visible keypoints) is scored once per run, on the checkpoint that validation picks. PCK at 0.05 (the share of visible keypoints within 0.05 of the face box's diagonal) is 0.86 overall with GPU image decoding, against 0.14 for a model-free control that places every point at its mean position in the box. The four pitch bands (camera 0 to 10, 10 to 20, 20 to 30 and 30 to 40 degrees below the face) score 0.72, 0.92, 0.88 and 0.88, masked images 0.88 and bare ones 0.84. The same recipe with CPU image decoding scores 0.50, with bands from 0.48 to 0.51. The two runs differ in the decoder. One of them was also restarted during training. The cause of the gap is unknown. The bar, set before training, is 0.80 overall and 0.60 in every band.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2500) 'Label quality: a second split of 480 renders (its own seed, sharing no image with the test, validation or first split) has a median camera fit of 0.118 px. 22 of the 480 sit over 1 px, 11 over 2 px, and the worst is 4.2 px. A larger fit residual puts the label that far from the drawn feature. A 2020 study of landmark annotation noise (arXiv 2007.15269) finds zero-mean noise of up to 3 percent of the box does not lower accuracy and raises output jitter, and 4.2 px is about 1.3 percent of the box diagonal (an estimate). All 600 images stay in the mix (operator, 2026-11-22).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2500) 'What was not measured
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2500) '- Whether any Hailo network parses, optimizes or compiles, and its distance from float.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2500) '- The skin patch with bending, a solid, a jaw with muscles, or a GPU run.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2500) '- The licence file inside the GNM weights, and the keypoint list.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2500) '- Any policy, the residual FSQ latent, and 2-bit weights, whose recipe is undisclosed.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2500) '- Reading the channel arrays back through OpenUSD. The guest reports counts and layer data.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2500) '- A live run on the operator's face, and the memory of the Hailo module in use.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2500) '- A second seed of the keypoint head, and any score from the 600-image mix run.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2500) 'Parked
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2500) 'Each item names why it waits and what restarts it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2500) '- Mix run: training on the 600 renders (the first 120 plus the second split) is paused after two of 40 epochs by a stop signal of unknown origin, and no score exists. It resumes when the operator releases it. Its best checkpoint is then scored once on the same 24 test renders and compared with the 0.86 above. More images and five times more optimizer steps change together, so a gain cannot be credited to the data alone.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2500) '- Decoder gap: the 0.50 and the 0.86 differ for a reason nobody has found. It resumes with a clean rerun of the CPU-decoding recipe, with no restart.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2500) '- Epoch timeline: AppSignal drops the last epoch span of a run in three runs, though the sender reports success. It resumes when the span timeline is needed. The integrated follower sends that span before the root span, which tests the guess that a late arrival is dropped.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-21T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2500) '- Portrait library: 1,499 AI-generated portraits under CC0, with a request not to redistribute the files. Projecting one onto a head as a texture is refused (operator, 2026-11-22). A mesh fitted from detected landmarks gives labels only as good as the detector, and a photograph has no truth to check against. It resumes after a landmark-driven fit on our own renders, where the truth is known, scores inside the 0.05 bar.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2500  1 LINE
 Text:Written
